# Default recipe on the Deepseek-V41-release-ced branch: CED-split PP2 prefill
# (dsv41-b300-1m.env, TP2 + TP2, is the alternative here).
#   docker compose -f compose.yaml --env-file dsv41-b300-1m-ced.env up --no-deps pd
# 2026-10-20, 4x B200, c24, 60 s (ced-perf): CED PP2 + TP2 decode served
# 5.05M TPM/GPU (TTFT 0.56/1.10/1.57 s, ITL p50 7.3 ms, 0 failed), up from
# 1.81M. The boundary handoff now reaches decode (it was lost on PP prefill and
# on prefill graph replay), so a tail runs layers 20-39 only. That B200 run
# replayed the full late graph (layers 21-39, index-source ops as breaks);
# B300 runs the tail eagerly (see the graph note below). Tail p50 ~45 ms on
# B200. Retrieval 40/40, as non-CED.
# UNQUALIFIED: built from B200 measurements; no B300 boot yet,
# and the CED-split PP2 prefill has not been rerun since the upstream merge.
# Values run to the end of the line; no shell expansion.

DSV41_IMAGE=dsv41-pd:latest
DSV41_MODEL=/data/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash
DSV41_DATA=/data/dsv41-bringup

# Two CED-split prefill workers, each a two-stage pipeline over the encoder
# layers 0-20 only (TP1 per stage, stages 0-7 | 8-20, split at the kv_source
# layer 8, no DSpark): prefill0 GPUs 0-1, prefill1 GPUs 2-3. Two TP2/EP2 decode
# workers with DSpark replay each prompt's tail through every layer: decode0
# GPUs 4-5, decode1 GPUs 6-7. Router 8040; prefill 8041-8042 (bootstrap
# 8999-9000); decode 8043-8044. Both roles route by X-SMG-Routing-Key (manual),
# so a conversation keeps its prefill prefix cache and decode on one worker.
GPUS=0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7
PORT=8040
BOOTSTRAP_PORT=8999
NCCL_PORT=29600
ROUTER_METRICS_PORT=29001
# The bench profile's oracle-proxy targets one prefill/decode pair only.
PREFILL_PORT=8041
DECODE_PORT=8043
ORACLE_PROXY_PORT=8034

# dsv41.env's serving flags with these changes for B300 and 1M context:
# --memory-profile B300 sizes both pools from HBM (auto). An encoder stage
# holds 57 / 91 GiB of weights, so the shared prefill pool is ~124M tokens
# (stage 8-20 binds, ~10 GiB left; stage 0-7 keeps ~156 GiB free); a TP2 decode
# rank holds ~55M tokens, capped by --mem-fraction. All estimates until the
# first B300 boot (the HBM figure is nominal until preflight sees memory.total).
# With ~117 1M-token contexts resident on prefill GPUs, HiCache is a small
# per-stage host tier: 32 GiB x 2 stages x 2 workers = 128 GiB host RAM, on top
# of the ~189 GiB Engram holder. SGLANG_ENABLE_DISAGG_PREFILL_EARLY_RESULT is
# not set: pipeline parallelism turns the overlap loop off, where it applies.
# Both roles wait up to 20 min for a KV handoff (default 5): a 1M request queued
# behind other cold 1M prefills can exceed 300 s before its transfer completes.
# Prefill graphs stay capped at 65536 (2026-10-20): with the cap following
# --context-length (131072) plus the eager-indexer memory changes, prefill hit a
# CUDA illegal memory access in graph replay under c24; either change alone ran
# clean (cap 65536: 5.51M TPM/GPU, TTFT 0.46/1.82/5.59 s). Root cause open.
# Fewer graph captures on B300 (2026-10-22): a lazy CED late-graph capture
# during c48 serving (rows=896) wedged a decode GPU's GSP (Xid 120/170), the
# capture-time firmware fault this rig also hits at startup. Decode therefore
# captures the late graph at startup for tails of 1-4 requests and nothing
# while serving (TAIL_GRAPH_PRECAPTURE_REQS), with the first replay of each
# size checked against eager; 1-8 (50 captures per decode worker) wedged a GPU
# at the eighth size. A tail replay is ~50 ms of mostly fixed overhead whether it
# carries 1 or 2 requests (c48 profile), so tails batch up to 4, waiting at most
# 30 ms (about three decode steps) to fill. Decode keeps each conversation's KV
# (decode radix): 97% of the prompt is reused and needle recall stayed 32/32.
# Startup also captures 3 prefill sizes (1024, 4096, chunk) and 5 decode sizes
# (1, 4, 16, 32, 64) instead of 7 and 10. Eager tails served 3.16M TPM/GPU at
# c48 (0 failed); late graphs pre-captured for 1-8 served 4.82M.
# Prefill keeps a 32 GiB transient reserve: at 16, stage 8-20 logged
# allocator OOM retries under c48.
DSV41_LAUNCH_ARGS=--gpu-models B300,GB300 --memory-profile B300 --num-prefill 2 --num-decode 2 --ced-split --prefill-pp 2 --context-length 1048576 --chunk-size 12288 --prefill-requests 16 --prefill-schedule-policy hrrn --decode-requests 64 --decode-radix-cache --decode-graph-bs 1,4,16,32 --prefill-graph-bs 1024,4096 --decode-polling-interval 2 --tokenizer-workers 4 --prefill-swa-prefix-tails 256 --max-total-tokens auto --prefill-hicache-size-gib 32 --prefill-transient-reserve-gib 32 --decode-max-total-tokens auto --mem-fraction 0.92 --custom-all-reduce on --prefill-graph-max-seq-len 65536 --prefill-env SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_ENGRAM_STAGING_PREFETCH=1 --prefill-env SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_GATHER_THREADS=8 --prefill-env NCCL_PROTO=LL128 --prefill-env SGLANG_FLASHINFER_AUTOTUNE_EXTEND=1 --prefill-env SGLANG_HRRN_SIZE_EXPONENT=1.5 --prefill-env SGLANG_OPT_PREFIX_PROMPT_ENCODE=1 --decode-env SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_ENGRAM_STAGING_PREFETCH=1 --decode-env SGLANG_DSV41_ENGRAM_GATHER_THREADS=8 --decode-env SGLANG_OPT_PREFIX_PROMPT_ENCODE=1 --compact-host-memory --kernel-cache-dir /data/dsv41-bringup/container-cache/dsv41-pd-b300 --prefill-env SGLANG_DISAGGREGATION_WAITING_TIMEOUT=1200 --decode-env SGLANG_DISAGGREGATION_WAITING_TIMEOUT=1200 --prefill-env SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_CED_BOUNDARY_HANDOFF=1 --decode-env SGLANG_OPT_DSV41_CED_BOUNDARY_HANDOFF=1 --decode-env SGLANG_DSV41_CED_TAIL_LATE_GRAPH=1 --decode-env SGLANG_DSV41_CED_TAIL_ENCODER_GRAPH=1 --decode-env SGLANG_DSV41_CED_TAIL_GRAPH_PRECAPTURE_REQS=1,2,3,4 --decode-env SGLANG_DSV41_CED_TAIL_BATCH_SIZE=4 --decode-env SGLANG_DSV41_CED_TAIL_MAX_WAIT_MS=30 --decode-env SGLANG_DSV41_CED_TAIL_GRAPH_CHECK=1 --decode-env SGLANG_DSV41_CED_GRAPH_MIN_FREE_GB=8
DSV41_EXTRA_ARGS=
